description:
In src/parser/jsonl.rs JsonlParser::parse_line(), immediately AFTER the envelope unwrap block (the let (working_json, envelope_json) = ... binding) and BEFORE the include_types/exclude_types checks, insert an early-return guard:

    // If unwrap produced a null payload (skip/meta routing), bail out early
    // before falling through to field extraction which would hard-error.
    if working_json.is_null() {
        return Ok(Vec::new());
    }

This handles the (Value::Null, _) tuples returned by unwrap_envelope for skip, meta, unknown-routing, and missing/non-object payload_field cases — preventing fall-through to timestamp extraction which would otherwise emit a hard 'Timestamp field not found' error.

Acceptance:
- The guard is present in parse_line() between the unwrap binding and the type-filter checks.
- working_json.is_null() returns Ok(Vec::new()) with no field extraction attempted.
- Code compiles (cargo check) with no new warnings.

The reflection use case needs quantitative behavioral metrics per session. Currently enrichment produces qualitative outputs (outcome, summary, anti-patterns). Missing: counts and rates that let a reflection tool spot patterns.

## New: BehavioralSignals struct (src/enrichment/behavioral_signals.rs)

pub struct BehavioralSignals {
    /// Total tool calls in session
    pub tool_call_count: u32,
    /// Tool call counts broken down by tool name
    pub tool_call_counts_by_name: HashMap<String, u32>,
    /// Files read more than once in the same session (re-read pattern)
    pub re_read_files: Vec<String>,
    /// Number of re-read events
    pub re_read_count: u32,
    /// Bash commands that returned non-zero exit code
    pub bash_failure_count: u32,
    /// Files written/edited more than once (possible revert pattern)
    pub multi_edit_files: Vec<String>,
    /// Approximate session duration in seconds (last_ts - first_ts)
    pub duration_secs: u64,
    /// Ratio: assistant turns / total turns
    pub assistant_turn_ratio: f32,
    /// Whether agent read any config/memory files (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .needle/, memory/)
    pub read_config_files: Vec<String>,
    /// Whether agent wrote/edited any config/memory files
    pub modified_config_files: Vec<String>,
    /// Number of times agent switched working directory (cwd changes in events)
    pub cwd_switch_count: u32,
}

## Integration
- Add to EnrichmentResult (src/enrichment/mod.rs)
- Store as behavioral_signals.json sidecar alongside the session JSONL:
  ~/.agentscribe/sessions/<agent>/<session_id>.behavioral.json
- Include behavioral_signals in search result JSON output (--json mode)

## Config file detection
Files matching any of these patterns are 'config/memory files':
- **/CLAUDE.md, **/AGENTS.md, **/.claude/**, **/.needle/**, **/memory/*.md, **/docs/notes/*.md

## Acceptance Criteria
- BehavioralSignals computed during enrichment for every session
- Sidecar file written alongside session JSONL
- Included in search --json output
- Tests: session with re-reads detected, bash failure counted, config file read detected
